From 5503075f0f36f4e66db1cc9fadac5a43ad780ef5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:45:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CR3: the gene lists grow to their live counts; the gene's new
 look fields get creator rows, reach the renderer and persist

- part catalog: live values must be 0..N-1; doomo_part_live[] (resident) gives every gene list's live
  count (part_live_count) and part_live_drawable() what this build can draw (the PS1 has no part VM
  until CR10: its creator offers the painted values only); slot gate= for the shape gate; review.txt
  sign-off lines are required for every live part not yet frozen
- resident_sanitize keeps every live choice; the classic generators keep rolling v1 values (Classic
  towns unchanged)
- the gene's eleven new fields (pupil, sclera, fur pattern / colour 3, glasses, outer, legwear, blush
  style, ear fold, hood up, handedness) ride in the resolved set (look_gene.c look_gene_deep) to every
  renderer path: portrait / body / fighter of a resident, figure_image_res for game callers,
  figure_image_d / portrait_image_look_d / fighter_render_d for the creator's draft; the cache key
  hashes the set (0 for a Classic look)
- saves are still the v1 wire image, which has no bits for them: the creator's NICK chunk carries
  them (and the high bit of aura, print and eye count) as a trailer, version 1 kept so an older
  build still reads the nicknames
- creator: rows for pupils, eye whites, ear fold, blush style, fur pattern + spot colour, outer layer
  + colour, legwear + colour, glasses, hood, handed paw, with help lines; part rows count and name
  from the catalog; the preview carries the set; cameras for glasses / hood / legwear
- part VM: anchor=frame blocks drawn in a frame the slot's hook sets (an eye, a brow, the nose, the
  mouth, a cheek, the pair of eyes, a leg); hooks for pupils, eye whites, blush, glasses, legwear,
  outer layers, fur patterns; scripted eyes and mouths hand emoting expressions to the painter
- icons: gene-only slots drawn; the PS1's packed set holds only what it can draw
- flipped live with review sign-offs: the wave-2 pupils, eye whites, glasses, blush, ear folds, the
  six B76 halos and CR2's family batch (12 hats, the sash, the satchel, the pearls): 42 parts

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
